---
/**
 * Believable 4–5 paragraph article about turbo lag for the desktop reader mock.
 * Uses Newsreader ~18px, narrow column, in-place diagram, removable sponsor block, and jumping footnote references.
 */
import { Trash } from "@lucide/astro";
---

<article class="article-body serif" id="reader-article">
  <header class="article-meta">
    <h1 class="article-title serif">
      How turbo lag actually works: inertia, boost threshold and transient response
    </h1>
    <div class="article-byline">
      <span>Marcus Vance</span>
      <span class="meta-sep">/</span>
      <span class="nums">Oct 2026</span>
      <span class="meta-sep">/</span>
      <span class="nums">5 min read</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <p class="article-p" id="p-1">
    The difference between boost threshold and turbo lag is often misunderstood in automotive
    engineering. Boost threshold is the engine speed below which the exhaust gas volume lacks
    sufficient enthalpy to spin the turbine fast enough to produce positive manifold pressure, no
    matter how wide the throttle is held open.
    <mark class="reader-mark pre-marked" data-hl-id="hl-1"
      ><span class="mark-inner"
        >Turbo lag, by contrast, is the transient delay between opening the throttle when operating
        above the boost threshold and the turbocharger reaching full boost</span
      ></mark
    ><sup class="fn-ref"><a href="#ref-1" id="fnref-1" class="fn-link" title="Jump to reference 1">1</a></sup>.
  </p>

  <p class="article-p" id="p-2">
    This transient delay is governed primarily by the rotational inertia of the rotating
    assembly—the compressor wheel, turbine wheel, and connecting shaft. Because rotational inertia
    scales with the fourth power of the wheel radius, even a modest reduction in wheel diameter
    yields dramatic reductions in spool-up delay<sup class="fn-ref"
      ><a href="#ref-2" id="fnref-2" class="fn-link" title="Jump to reference 2">2</a></sup
    >. Modern performance designs employ lightweight titanium-aluminide turbine wheels and ceramic
    ball bearings to cut physical spool inertia by more than forty percent compared to traditional
    journal-bearing cast Inconel wheels.
  </p>

  <figure class="reader-figure">
    <div class="figure-graphic">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 540 180"
        fill="none"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        class="chart-svg"
        aria-label="Graph comparing boost response curves over time"
      >
        <!-- Grid lines -->
        <line x1="60" y1="20" x2="60" y2="140" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1"></line>
        <line x1="60" y1="140" x2="500" y2="140" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1"></line>
        <line x1="60" y1="80" x2="500" y2="80" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-dasharray="3 3" stroke-width="1"></line>
        <line x1="60" y1="20" x2="500" y2="20" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-dasharray="3 3" stroke-width="1"></line>

        <!-- Labels -->
        <text x="52" y="144" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" font-family="var(--font-sans)">0 bar</text>
        <text x="52" y="84" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" font-family="var(--font-sans)">0.8 bar</text>
        <text x="52" y="24" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" font-family="var(--font-sans)">1.6 bar</text>
        <text x="60" y="158" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="11" font-family="var(--font-sans)">0.0s (Throttle)</text>
        <text x="220" y="158" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="11" font-family="var(--font-sans)">0.6s</text>
        <text x="380" y="158" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="11" font-family="var(--font-sans)">1.2s</text>

        <!-- Twin-scroll curve (faster response) -->
        <path
          d="M 60 140 C 110 138, 140 70, 240 24 L 500 22"
          stroke="var(--foreground)"
          stroke-width="2.5"
          fill="none"
        ></path>
        <circle cx="240" cy="24" r="4" fill="var(--foreground)"></circle>
        <text x="252" y="32" fill="var(--foreground)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" font-family="var(--font-sans)">
          Twin-scroll (0.58s to peak)
        </text>

        <!-- Single open scroll curve (slower lag) -->
        <path
          d="M 60 140 C 170 140, 240 100, 390 24 L 500 24"
          stroke="var(--muted-foreground)"
          stroke-width="1.75"
          stroke-dasharray="4 3"
          fill="none"
        ></path>
        <text x="396" y="44" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="11" font-family="var(--font-sans)">
          Open volute (1.12s)
        </text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
      Figure 1: Manifold boost pressure rise following throttle step at 3,400 RPM. Split turbine
      scrolls isolate exhaust pulses to spool the wheel faster.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- Removable sponsor block -->
  <div class="removable-block" id="sponsor-block" data-removable="true">
    <div class="removable-inner">
      <div class="removable-top">
        <span class="removable-badge">Sponsor read</span>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="remove-inline-btn"
          id="remove-sponsor-action"
          title="Remove sponsor read from article"
        >
          <Trash size={13} stroke-width={1.75} />
          <span>Remove text</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <p class="removable-text">
        This teardown is supported by Apex Flow Ceramic Coatings. Protect turbine housings against
        thermal oxidation and keep exhaust gas kinetic energy inside the manifold. Use code
        TURBO15 for testing samples.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="article-p" id="p-3">
    Exhaust manifold volume also plays a decisive role in throttle response. Long, large-diameter
    tubular headers expand the total volume that exhaust gases must pressurize before reaching the
    turbine housing nozzle. Short-runner exhaust manifolds, or cylinder heads with integrated exhaust
    collectors surrounded by cooling jackets, shrink this pre-turbine volume and sharpen transient
    throttle response significantly<sup class="fn-ref"
      ><a href="#ref-3" id="fnref-3" class="fn-link" title="Jump to reference 3">3</a></sup
    >.
  </p>

  <p class="article-p" id="p-4">
    When sizing a turbocharger, matching the compressor map and turbine housing area-to-radius ratio
    (A/R) to the engine displacement ensures reliable boost without choking top-end breathing or
    causing compressor surge under rapid throttle closure.
  </p>

  <footer class="footnotes-section" id="footnotes">
    <div class="footnotes-divider"></div>
    <h3 class="footnotes-title sans">References cited</h3>
    <ol class="footnotes-list">
      <li id="ref-1" class="footnote-item">
        <span class="fn-number nums">1.</span>
        <span class="fn-text"
          >Watson, N. &amp; Janota, M. (1982). <em>Turbocharging the Internal Combustion Engine</em>,
          Macmillan Press, pp. 45–62.</span
        >
        <a href="#fnref-1" class="fn-back" title="Back to text">↩ back</a>
      </li>
      <li id="ref-2" class="footnote-item">
        <span class="fn-number nums">2.</span>
        <span class="fn-text"
          >SAE Technical Paper 2004-01-0988: <em>Transient Response Modeling of Variable-Geometry
          Turbochargers</em>.</span
        >
        <a href="#fnref-2" class="fn-back" title="Back to text">↩ back</a>
      </li>
      <li id="ref-3" class="footnote-item">
        <span class="fn-number nums">3.</span>
        <span class="fn-text"
          >Baines, N. C. (2005). <em>Fundamentals of Turbocharging</em>, Concepts NREC, pp. 112–129.</span
        >
        <a href="#fnref-3" class="fn-back" title="Back to text">↩ back</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </footer>
</article>

<style>
  .article-body {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-size: 17.5px;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--foreground);
    user-select: text;
    -webkit-user-select: text;
  }

  .article-meta {
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .article-title {
    font-size: clamp(21px, 2.8vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .article-byline {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .meta-sep {
    color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .article-p {
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Footnote link styling */
  .fn-ref {
    font-size: 0.72em;
    line-height: 0;
    vertical-align: super;
    padding-inline: 2px;
  }

  .fn-link {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 1px 3px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transition: background-color 140ms var(--ease-out), color 140ms var(--ease-out);
  }

  .fn-link:hover {
    color: var(--foreground);
    background: var(--muted);
  }

  /* In-place figure */
  .reader-figure {
    margin: 32px 0;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--card);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .figure-graphic {
    padding: 18px 16px 12px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--muted) 45%, var(--card));
  }

  .chart-svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .figure-caption {
    padding: 10px 16px 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  /* Removable sponsor block */
  .removable-block {
    margin: 26px 0;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--muted) 55%, var(--card));
    padding: 14px 18px;
    transition:
      height 300ms var(--ease-out),
      opacity 240ms var(--ease-out),
      margin 300ms var(--ease-out),
      padding 300ms var(--ease-out);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .removable-block.is-removed {
    height: 0 !important;
    opacity: 0 !important;
    margin-top: 0 !important;
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    padding-top: 0 !important;
    padding-bottom: 0 !important;
    border-color: transparent !important;
  }

  .removable-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .removable-badge {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .remove-inline-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 140ms var(--ease-out), color 140ms var(--ease-out);
  }

  .remove-inline-btn:hover {
    color: var(--destructive);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--destructive) 10%, transparent);
  }

  .removable-text {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  /* Marks in reader */
  :global(.reader-mark) {
    background-color: var(--marker-soft);
    color: inherit;
    padding-inline: 0.12em;
    margin-inline: -0.12em;
    border-radius: 0.14em;
    transition: background-color 220ms var(--ease-out);
  }

  :global(.reader-mark.pulse-flash) {
    animation: markerPulse 1.2s var(--ease-out);
  }

  @keyframes markerPulse {
    0% {
      background-color: var(--marker-strong);
    }
    100% {
      background-color: var(--marker-soft);
    }
  }

  /* Footnotes */
  .footnotes-section {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .footnotes-divider {
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    width: 120px;
  }

  .footnotes-title {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--foreground);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .footnotes-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .footnote-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    transition: background-color 300ms var(--ease-out);
  }

  .footnote-item.flash-highlight {
    background-color: var(--marker-soft);
  }

  .fn-number {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--foreground);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .fn-text {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .fn-back {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 12px;
    margin-left: 6px;
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .fn-back:hover {
    color: var(--foreground);
    background: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
